{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYFyqRiK8tDYHcxeyACQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The README already says the autumn policy: \"the loan period for every kind of item is 21 days.\" So there's nothing to change there.\n\nThe mismatch is in the code. `LOAN_DAYS` in `loans.py` still has the old periods:\n\n| kind | now | policy |\n|---|---|---|\n| novel | 14 | 21 |\n| magazine | 7 | 21 |\n| dvd | 7 | 21 |\n| tool | 5 | 21 |\n| reference | 3 | 21 |\n\nThe existing tests also assert the old values (`novel` is 14 days, `dvd` is 7). The desk screen uses this code, so patrons currently get the old due dates.\n\nDo you want me to change `LOAN_DAYS` to 21 for all kinds? If yes, I would do four things:\n- Update the two existing tests to 21 days.\n- Add a test that checks every kind in `LOAN_DAYS` returns 21 days. It would fail before the change and pass after.\n- Leave the README alone. I could also add a line to it listing the kinds.\n- Run the full test suite before and after. `pytest` isn't installed here, so I'd use `python -m unittest`.\n\nI haven't changed any files. I didn't assume the code change was wanted, because it changes the due dates patrons see. If the README was meant to say something different, tell me what it should say."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":413,"cache_read_input_tokens":39278,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":413},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e39e2e39-180a-4f5a-90c3-bf9a97cac41b","uuid":"acbe51d0-eaab-4882-b1e3-52d9cadaf61f","timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:24:50.186Z","request_id":"req_011CgYFyq6cs5oyErMUmS42K"}
